@Megan Daniel Not pressing, but a follow up question: 
When you rename name.ext to NAME.ext or name.EXT, it currently will serve an error saying that already exists. This is due to an implementation issue. I tried replicating the same issue on Files app and on Chrome, it also won't allow renaming. I'm wondering if there is a better error we can serve. As a user it does seem weird that the error says "A file named "name.EXT already exists" when technically the existing file is called name.ext.

Let me know what you think. Thanks!
